 CEO & Director | Age 61 | Compensation: $3.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 801 people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 11%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $30K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Virtus Investment Partners, Inc is a small-cap financial services business with a $730M market cap on $853M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 9% cost of capital, a 3-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The company is burning through $74M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 8.8\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 17.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 6.5% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 9% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $3.7M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-3736437.69},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 40% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 43% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","11 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Trading the Move, Not the Narrative: (VRTS) Edition","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/40/Trading_the_Move,_Not_the_Narrative:_VRTS_Edition_112426045001_1795513801.html","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795513801.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Asset Managers' AUM Trends Mixed in October: VCTR, LAZ, VRTS & IVZ in Focus","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/asset-managers-aum-trends-mixed-123600689.html","date":"2026-11-18","timestamp":1795005360.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.44,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Virtus Investment Partners Declares Quarterly Cash Dividend on Common Stock","source":"businesswire.com","link":"http://www.businesswire